    "section": "generative",
    "blurb": "Hundreds of luminous points orbit at integer harmonic ratios, collapsing into kaleidoscopic crystalline symmetries and unravelling into drifting phosphor dust.",
    "prompt": "Harmonic motion in the manner of John Whitney's computer films: hundreds of points each rotating at a whole-number multiple of a base speed, sweeping through moments of perfect symmetry and back into scattered clouds. Make it striking on a big projected wall in a dark room: a bold composition, rich colour against real blacks, depth, glow, and motion that reads from across the room. Keep a demoscener's economy: lookup tables and fixed-size buffers kept in room.state, low-resolution offscreen buffers for any per-pixel work, nothing allocated inside hot loops, a steady 60fps at 1920x1080, and compact, clearly named code.",
